   "not injected" branch called the generic _add_credential_leak_vulnerability
   (which now could never include the goal), instead of deterministically
   seeding the goal's own credentials. Reverted.

3. THIS commit fixes both problems together: (a) excludes goals from the
   fallback pool in BOTH SolvabilityPostProcessor and
   SolvabilityConstraintProcessor (the latter is a separate, earlier-running
   "stale fork" duplicate with the identical bug - this was NOT caught in
   the first attempt, since only SPP was fixed then), (b) makes
   _ensure_goal_reachable()'s fallback deterministic instead of
   probabilistic.

